<section class="hero" style="min-height:340px">
  <img class="bg" src="../assets/pics/hub-arc-corridor.jpg" alt="">
  <div class="veil"></div>
  <div class="wrap inner">
    <div class="eyebrow">Orientation</div>
    <h1>How to use this site</h1>
    <p class="sub">Two minutes here saves fumbling later — how the modes, saving, exports and your paper workbook fit together.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<main class="stub wrap" id="main">
  <div class="howgrid" style="margin-top:34px">

    <div class="how">
      <div class="hn">01 · MODES</div>
      <h3>Self-paced vs Present</h3>
      <p>The <kbd class="ui">Self-paced</kbd> / <kbd class="ui">Present</kbd> toggle lives top-right on every page. <b>Self-paced</b> shows the full explanatory prose from the Concepts Workbook — use it for pre-reading, catch-up or revisiting after the course. <b>Present</b> strips pages back to the essentials for the live room, where your facilitator carries the narrative.</p>
      <p>Your choice is remembered on this device.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="how">
      <div class="hn">02 · SAVING</div>
      <h3>Your answers save themselves</h3>
      <p>Every field autosaves as you type — watch for the <kbd class="ui">✓ Saved automatically</kbd> pill bottom-right. There are no accounts and no servers: <b>everything stays in this browser on this device</b>. Nothing you write leaves your machine unless you export it yourself.</p>
      <p>That privacy has one consequence: a different browser or device starts empty — which is what the next card solves.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="how">
      <div class="hn">03 · TWO DAYS, ANY DEVICE</div>
      <h3>Carry your answers with you</h3>
      <p>At the end of Day 1 (or any time), download your answers as a single file. Load it tomorrow — on the same laptop, a different one, or a tablet — and you continue exactly where you stopped. The file is named after your workflow, e.g. <span style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px">aal-evidence-complaint-triage-pilot.json</span>.</p>
      <div class="btnrow"><button class="btn primary" data-action="download-state">Download my answers</button>
      <button class="btn ghost" data-action="load-state">Load answers</button></div>
    </div>

    <div class="how">
      <div class="hn">04 · ARTEFACTS</div>
      <h3>Your work becomes documents</h3>
      <p>Each module assembles your answers into a named artefact — the Boundary Map, the Governance Cadence Map, and so on — with a <kbd class="ui">Download PDF</kbd> button (choose “Save as PDF” in the print dialog). The <a href="evidence-pack.html" style="color:var(--teal-dark);font-weight:600">Evidence Pack</a> collects all eight into one exportable document: your defence.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="how">
      <div class="hn">05 · YOUR PAPER WORKBOOK</div>
      <h3>Matched to the Activity Workbook</h3>
      <p>Activity numbers here are identical to the fillable PDF — Activity 3.1 is <i>Where Is Your Line?</i> in both. Work wherever suits you; if you write on paper in the room, you can transfer the answers that matter here so they flow into your Evidence Pack.</p>
      <p>The workflow you choose in Activity 1.3 follows you everywhere — look for the chip in the header.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="how">
      <div class="hn">06 · REFERENCE &amp; RESET</div>
      <h3>The A–Z, and starting over</h3>
      <p>The <kbd class="ui">A–Z</kbd> button (top-right) opens the five foundational definitions from anywhere — automation, generative AI, agents, agentic AI, autonomy — with a link to drill them in the <a href="foundations.html" style="color:var(--teal-dark);font-weight:600">Foundations Gym</a>.</p>
      <p>Starting over erases every answer in this browser. It asks first, and download-before-reset is always the safe move.</p>
      <div class="btnrow"><button class="btn" data-action="reset-state">Start over</button></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="buildnote" style="margin-top:18px"><b>One technical note.</b> This site is built to be hosted; if you're opening the files directly from a folder (a <span style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px">file://</span> address), some browsers limit saving between pages. Use the hosted address your facilitator shares.</div>

  <div class="pn">
    <a href="welcome.html"><span class="lbl">← Previous</span><span>Welcome &amp; Orientation</span></a>
    <a class="next" href="foundations.html"><span class="lbl">Next →</span><span>The Foundations Gym</span></a>
  </div>
</main>

